{{/*
  The catalog, with the search moved into the header.

  This file overrides two names in the catalog's own template set and leaves the
  rest of pages/products.gohtml — products_filters, products_list, products_pager —
  coming from the defaults, because an override replaces the definitions it names
  and nothing else.

    content    the page, without the filter form above the grid.
    nav_extra  the same form, in the header's Search dropdown.

  Defining nav_extra *here* is what keeps it off every other page: this file is
  parsed into the catalog's set alone, so the block stays empty on the cart, the
  checkout and the error pages — which is what the layout wants, since none of
  their page data carries .Search or .Facets.
*/}}
{{define "content"}}
<h1>All products</h1>

<div id="products">
  {{template "products_list" .}}
</div>
{{end}}

{{define "nav_extra"}}{{template "products_filters" .}}{{end}}
